      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DEVILS I (3) stepped up to 1200m last start and was too good at this track, scoring by 1.4L. He's a track and trip winner in the past and he looks ready for this distance now. Maps to get every chance under Faithfull and can bring up back-to-back wins. CORN COB (1) bolted in two back before finding them a little slick over the 1200m journey here most recently. Should be better suited here and the claim of Webster comes in handy. Won well here three starts ago and he can make an impression. LACEVINSKY (2) was fresh from a break of eight months last start when beaten 1.5 lengths into fourth over 1200m at this track. Has three wins at the trip. One of the better chances. RED REBEL (6) finished second last time over 1406m at Roebourne, beaten 3.5 lengths. Will trim down following recent racing. Suitably placed so anticipating another forward showing. WHO'S YOUR MAMA (7) is better than she showed last time out and can feature.",
